# Test: enum-refusal-inline-leaf-list
#
# QUESTION: does `ze config validate` refuse a leaf-list member outside the
# enumeration, written alone or inside a bracket, with the enum refusal for
# that member: the full path named once, the values with help in declared
# order, and the file-form fix, never `(valid: ...)`?
# A unit test drives storeValueOrArray over a test schema; this proves the
# shipped YANG leaf-list reaches the same arm through the real entry point.
#
# Leaf: ospf router-information scope, a YANG leaf-list of an enumeration
#   (internal/plugins/ospf/yang/ze-ospf-conf.yang: link, area, as, each with a
#   ze:help). A leaf-list with no ze:syntax is a ValueOrArrayNode, so both the
#   single-value and the bracket spelling end in storeValueOrArray
#   (internal/component/config/parser_list.go), whose fix is `scope <...>;`.
#
# No shipped leaf is an enum-typed inline-list child, MultiLeafNode,
# BracketLeafListNode or freeform attribute: those arms are proven on the test
# schema by TestInlineLeafListEnumRefusal and TestEveryValueArmNamesTheFullPath
# (internal/component/config/value_refusal_test.go).
#
# VALIDATES: spec-config-enum-refusal-proposes-valid-values AC-5 (the shipped
#   leaf-list arms), with the accepted control.
# PREVENTS: `(valid: link, area, as)`, `invalid enum`, a refusal naming the
#   leaf-list without its path, or one with no fix line.

stdin=single:terminator=EOF_SINGLE
ospf {
	router-id 10.0.0.1
	router-information {
		scope bogus
	}
}
EOF_SINGLE

stdin=bracket:terminator=EOF_BRACKET
ospf {
	router-id 10.0.0.1
	router-information {
		scope [ link bogus ]
	}
}
EOF_BRACKET

stdin=accepted:terminator=EOF_ACCEPTED
ospf {
	router-id 10.0.0.1
	router-information {
		scope [ link area ]
	}
	areas {
		area 0.0.0.0 {
		}
	}
}
EOF_ACCEPTED

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=single
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=line 4: ospf router-information scope: "bogus" is not an accepted value
expect=stdout:pattern=scope accepts only these values:\n +link  Link-local \(OSPFv2 opaque type 9\)\.\n +area  Area \(OSPFv2 opaque type 10, OSPFv3 0xA00C\)\.\n +as    AS-wide \(OSPFv2 opaque type 11, OSPFv3 0xC00C\)\.\n *fix: scope <link\|area\|as>;
reject=stdout:contains=(valid:
reject=stdout:contains=invalid enum
reject=stdout:contains=expected one of

cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=bracket
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=line 4: ospf router-information scope: "bogus" is not an accepted value
expect=stdout:pattern=scope accepts only these values:\n +link  Link-local
expect=stdout:contains=fix: scope <link|area|as>;
reject=stdout:contains=(valid:
reject=stdout:contains=invalid enum
reject=stdout:contains=expected one of

# The control declares an area, as the committed OSPF parse configs do
# (test/parse/redistribute-tag-filter.ci), so only the scope members decide it.
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=accepted
expect=exit:code=0
reject=stdout:contains=is not an accepted value
